# The DroneCAN page's Inspector (Controls/DroneCANInspector.cs) and its Subscriber
# (Controls/DroneCANSubscriber.cs), over MAVLinkCAN1 to the SITL copter: the page's own node,
# 127, is the only one on a forwarded bus SITL has no DroneCAN node on, and the Inspector hears
# the node's NodeStatus as the C#'s hears its own sent messages (MessageReceived raised for
# them). The tree: "ID 127", then "ID 127 - org.missionplanner ~nBps" (Update, :56-117); under
# it the type's node, "uavcan_protocol_NodeStatus (r.r Hz, #341) ~nBps"; under that the fields
# as PopulateMSG lays them out, with the .NET type (:119-200). A field selected enables Graph It
# and Subscribe (:326-346); Graph It asks "Points of history?" and opens a graph of the field,
# filling as messages come (:347-446); Subscribe opens the Subscriber, whose combo lists the
# types heard and whose box gets each NodeStatus as JSON (DroneCANSubscriber.cs:88-131).
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760. Run as
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-dronecan-inspector.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env MP_LOG_DIR $WORK
screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 44

expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click tab-setup
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigDroneCAN
expect setup.page ConfigDroneCAN
expect config.dronecan.active true
expect config.dronecan.inspector.window false
expect config.dronecan.inspector.opened 0

# Inspector before a bus: "Please connect first".
click dronecan-inspector
expect config.dronecan.inspector.window false
expect status Please connect first

# MAVLinkCAN1, and the node up.
click dronecan-interface
click dronecan-interface-list-1
expect config.dronecan.interface MAVLinkCAN1
click dronecan-connect
expect config.dronecan.connected true
expect config.dronecan.bus MAVLinkCAN1
expect config.dronecan.nodes 1
expect config.dronecan.node.127.name org.missionplanner

# The Inspector: the tree fills from the node's own NodeStatus.
click dronecan-inspector
expect config.dronecan.inspector.window true
expect config.dronecan.inspector.opened 1
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graphit false
expect config.dronecan.inspector.subscribe false
expect config.dronecan.inspector.history 50
expect config.dronecan.inspector.prompt none
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graphs 0
expect config.dronecan.inspector.heard > 0
expect config.dronecan.inspector.updates > 1
expect config.dronecan.inspector.row.0 ~ ID 127 - org.missionplanner ~
expect config.dronecan.inspector.row.0 ~ Bps
click dronecan-inspector-toggle-127
# Under it a node per type the node has sent since the Inspector opened: its NodeStatus each
# second, and - on the next wall-clock second that is a multiple of ten - its answer to its own
# GetNodeInfo poll, DroneCAN.cs:313-360 asking each node of its list in turn, itself among them,
# and MessageReceived raised for its own messages. The tree sorted by text (treeView1.Sort()),
# the answer is above NodeStatus. Waited for, so the rows are the same whenever the run starts.
within 12
expect config.dronecan.inspector.rows 3
expect config.dronecan.inspector.row.1 ~ uavcan_protocol_GetNodeInfo_res (
expect config.dronecan.inspector.row.1 ~ , #1) ~
expect config.dronecan.inspector.row.2 ~ uavcan_protocol_NodeStatus (
expect config.dronecan.inspector.row.2 ~ , #341) ~
click dronecan-inspector-toggle-127-341
expect config.dronecan.inspector.rows 8
expect config.dronecan.inspector.type.127.341.uptime_sec UInt32
expect config.dronecan.inspector.type.127.341.health Byte
expect config.dronecan.inspector.type.127.341.vendor_specific_status_code UInt16
expect config.dronecan.inspector.value.127.341.uptime_sec > 0

# A field selected: Graph It and Subscribe enabled, the path as selectedmsgid.
click dronecan-inspector-node-127-341-uptime_sec
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graphit true
expect config.dronecan.inspector.subscribe true
expect config.dronecan.inspector.selected 127/341/uptime_sec

# Graph It: the question, its default 50, a graph of uptime_sec filling at 1 Hz.
click dronecan-inspector-graphit
expect config.dronecan.inspector.prompt Points of history?
click dronecan-inspector-points-ok
expect config.dronecan.inspector.prompt none
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graphs 1
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graphit false
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graph.0.curves uptime_sec
within 6
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graph.0.points > 1
click dronecan-inspector-graph-0-close
expect config.dronecan.inspector.graphs 0

# Subscribe: the Subscriber, its combo filled within a second, NodeStatus chosen, its JSON.
click dronecan-inspector-subscribe
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.window true
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.lines 100
# The types in the order heard: NodeStatus first, as each second's goes out before that second's
# GetNodeInfo poll, whose answer may follow while this waits.
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.items ~ uavcan_protocol_NodeStatus
click dronecan-subscriber-type
click dronecan-subscriber-type-0
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.type uavcan_protocol_NodeStatus
within 6
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.text.lines > 6
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.text ~ "uptime_sec":
click dronecan-subscriber-lines-up
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.lines 101
click dronecan-subscriber-close
expect config.dronecan.subscriber.window false

# Closed, and the bus left.
click dronecan-inspector-close
expect config.dronecan.inspector.window false
click dronecan-connect
expect config.dronecan.connected false
